# tdstmt.ref - Expected TMTOGO(KTIME) placement for PROGRAM TDSTMT
#
# Source of truth: FROZEN mis/xsem00.f (read-only) and mis/tmtogo.f.
# The modern dispatcher modern/dispatch/disptbl.f must preserve
# EXACTLY ONE pre-dispatch CALL TMTOGO(KTIME), mirroring the legacy
# single call at mis/xsem00.f L196 (250 CALL TMTOGO (KTIME)).
#
# Key/value lines (machine-readable). The driver tdstmt.f hardcodes
# these expectations and counts the calls via a local TMTOGO stub.
#
EXPECT_TMTOGO_CALLS 1
NOOP_MODX 25
ALT_NOOP_MODX 36
#
# Notes:
#  - The driver calls the dispatcher with a RESERVED no-op MODX (25)
#    so no module subroutine executes; only the single pre-dispatch
#    CALL TMTOGO is exercised, and must be called exactly once.
#  - mis/tmtogo.f: SUBROUTINE TMTOGO (TOGO); INTEGER TOGO. The driver
#    stub returns a large positive TOGO so the time-budget guard
#    (KTIME .LE. 0) is NOT taken.
#  - KTIME originates from /SYSTEM/ (declared in mis/SMCOMX.COM per
#    the AAP discrepancy flag); the driver does not declare /SYSTEM/
#    - the stub fills the passed argument.
#
# EXPECT_VERDICT PASS: TDSTMT
